  "worked_solution": "The range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n0\\le \\theta \\le \\pi .\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and second quadrants.\n\nSince $-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ is negative, our answer is an angle that lies in the second quadrant, where cosine is negative.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13964047/assets/a33ea7c6d1aa7cd7e54376aefb2af4347da59a61ecaabdbf4964d41b9661870a.png)\n\nFrom the values in the second quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})=-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arccos}\u2061(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.\n$$",
